---
import Docs from '../layouts/Docs.astro';import {tutorials} from '../data/tutorials';const prefix=Astro.url.pathname.startsWith('/light/')?'/light':'';
---
<Docs title="CSS Tutorials: Accordions, Headers & Card Grids" description="Build practical CSS-only components with original StyloftCSS tutorials, editable HTML examples and browser-support guidance." active="tutorials" section="docs"><header class="docs-page-header"><h1>Build something useful.</h1><p>Three practical tutorials connect semantic HTML, CSS classes and the decisions behind each component.</p></header><div class="sl-stack sl-gap-6">{tutorials.map(t=><article class="sl-card sl-stack sl-gap-4"><h2 class="sl-text-xl"><a href={prefix+'/tutorials/'+t.slug+'/'}>{t.title}</a></h2><p>{t.description}</p></article>)}</div><section class="guide-section"><h2>Before you start</h2><p><a href={prefix+'/guides/#installation'}>Download and load StyloftCSS</a>, then open a tutorial and copy the working HTML. The examples use native controls and CSS; the editable documentation playground is a separate website feature.</p></section></Docs>
